WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.930
<b>Never Dream</b>

3
00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.630
Captain! Captain!

4
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.350
[NAMI]
One tooth
is the size of our boat!

5
00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.180
That's it.

6
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.310
We're dead!

7
00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.160
There's no monster.

8
00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.900
This is a one big stupid dream that we're
all having together for some reason!

9
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.020
A dream! Right!

10
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.360
Ah, It was just a dream.

11
00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.600
[ROBIN]
You know...

12
00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.690
Our boys just got eaten.

13
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.110
So did that ship we
were trying to salvage.

14
00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.370
How can you be so calm?

15
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.700
Yep. Most definitely eaten.

16
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.080
I can see the air hoses
dangling from its jaws.

17
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.120
Stop!

18
00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.340
[CHOPPER screams]

19
00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.020
A sea monster
ate my friends!

20
00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:51.150
What am I gonna do?

21
00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.240
This is all your fault!

22
00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.570
You're the one who
said it would be safe

23
00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.660
at the bottom of the Grand Line.

24
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.120
I don't know, what qualifies
for "safe" in your book,

25
00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.000
but in mine it's not
man‐eating turtles!

26
00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.670
You're right.

27
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.820
Sorry!

28
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.870
That's as good as
it's going to get, I guess.

29
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.000
If we don't cut the air hoses,

30
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.210
that beast will drag us down
to the bottom of the ocean.

31
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.220
[USOPP screams]

32
00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.630
I don't care what you do,
just do something.

33
00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.180
You're the tough and smart lady!

34
00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.010
[ROBIN]
Give me a minute.

35
00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.930
I'll see what
I can come up with.

36
00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.280
[BLUE SHIRT]
Okay, boys!

37
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.150
Time to save our noble captain!

38
00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.280
Our pride, honor,
and lives are at stake here!

39
00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.530
[BLUE SHIRT]
Our captain
is alive and we will find him!

40
00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.370
Mark my words!

41
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.490
They're right.

42
00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.120
It's these challenging times
that prove the strength

43
00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.630
by which we are made.

44
00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:56.300
Usopp!

45
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.140
Cut the air hoses,
and get us out of here!

46
00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:01.910
[USOPP]
This is what we're made of?

47
00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.310
[CHOPPER]
Coward!

48
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.020
Huh? Huh?!

49
00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.020
What is that?

50
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.900
It's like everything got dark.

51
00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.020
Uh! Scary.

52
00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.570
There's no way.

53
00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.570
Why is it so dark?

54
00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.150
It's not that late.

55
00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.240
It's time to leave guys!

56
00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.160
Now!

57
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.580
Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!

58
00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:26.830
[PIRATE B]
This is a bad omen.

59
00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.420
We all know the suddenly
darkened sun is the harbinger

60
00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.710
of the monsters to soon rise.

61
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.210
[PIRATE C]
We gotta save
the boss and get outta here!

62
00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.310
Luffy!

63
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.640
Tell me what happened! Are you
dead?! Where're the others?

64
00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.390
[USOPP]
Zoro! Sanji!

65
00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:49.430
[ZORO]
Set sail now.

66
00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.560
We gotta get outta here!

67
00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.640
[SANJI]
Yeah. That guy's crazy.

68
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.560
I'm so glad you're okay.

69
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.560
Now let's get away

70
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.190
from this stinking turtle
as fast as we can!

71
00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.400
No, it wasn't a turtle.

72
00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.520
It was a monkey.

73
00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.610
Yeah, a bona fide sea monkey.

74
00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.340
Can't say I'm too surprised
that he and Luffy

75
00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.670
got along as well as they did.

76
00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.340
Well they're both monkeys!

77
00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.800
But when he caught a
glimpse of all this stuff

78
00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.720
that we had taken from his
ship, he totally flipped out

79
00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.320
and went on a rampage.

80
00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.410
I've never seen a primate
act like that before.

81
00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.700
Yeah, that's Masira,
the King of All Salvagers.

82
00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.910
But never mind him,

83
00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.400
how did the three of you escape
from the giant sea turtle?

84
00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.920
[ZORO]
Ugh! Why do you
keep talking about a turtle?

85
00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:24.840
[USOPP]
Hmm. That's weird.

86
00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:28.060
Now he's just floating
there like a statue,

87
00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.300
with his mouth gaping open.

88
00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.220
Oh I get it. Of course!
That's how you guys escaped!

89
00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.220
[ZORO, SANJI]
– We were in that thing's mouth??
– We were in that thing's mouth??

90
00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.580
[USOPP]
Nothing gets
past you guys does it?

91
00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.370
That's the turtle that ate
the ship you were inside!

92
00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.710
[coughs]

93
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.630
Hey. When did night happen?

94
00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.210
Attention, all hands!

95
00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.180
We're getting outta here now!

96
00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.470
[roars]

97
00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.720
Not so fast!

98
00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.770
Hand over the
treasure you stole.

99
00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:03.310
Or I'll tear your ship apart
and find all of it anyway!

100
00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.250
Is he right?

101
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:05.510
You guys found some treasure?

102
00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.680
[chuckles]
We sure did. Tons of it.

103
00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:09.720
[ZORO]
This isn't good.

104
00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:13.310
If he starts rampaging
the ship, we all go down.

105
00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:19.150
Hey, Captain, behind you!

106
00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.230
[MASIRA]
Hmm? What's behind me?

107
00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.840
– Sea monsters!
– Sea monsters!

108
00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.070
[ZORO]
That couldn't have been real.

109
00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:54.620
[USOPP]
Those things
were taller than the sky!

110
00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.250
The Grand Line is
an endless parade

111
00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.180
of mysteries and annoyance.

112
00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:04.150
I mean, look at the nightmare
of just making it through today.

113
00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.860
First there was that
a huge galleon that fell

114
00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.920
from the clouds on top of us.

115
00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.590
The Log Pose's needle
started pointing to the sky.

116
00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.130
A psycho make‐up
wearing monkey shows up

117
00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.640
and blocks our way.

118
00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.210
And then,
a gigantic sea turtle came

119
00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:18.520
and ate our salvage ship.

120
00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.190
Then darkness fell.

121
00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:22.840
Because the biggest
monsters I've ever seen

122
00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:26.010
in my life blocked out the sun.

123
00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.740
I must admit, even I was
intimidated by those things.

124
00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.640
[USOPP]
Those monsters were too
big for any of us to take them.

125
00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.010
[CHOPPER]
Yeah. If I never see them again,

126
00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:44.600
it would be a blessing.

127
00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:46.490
Don't sweat it.

128
00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:47.950
They're nothing.

129
00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:48.950
[CHOPPER]
Hmm?

130
00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.030
If I'd really cut loose,

131
00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.910
I could've taught those
sea monsters a thing or two.

132
00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.290
Really?

133
00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.240
Sure.

134
00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.500
I fought ten of those
things a while back.

135
00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.540
You fought ten of 'em?!

136
00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.500
[NAMI]
Come on, you guys!

137
00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.430
Tell me you at least tried to
find something down there

138
00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.450
that we could actually use!

139
00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.620
All you brought back was
a bunch of scattered junk!

140
00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:13.920
There's not a single clue here
about how to get to sky island!

141
00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.840
There wasn't
anything there, believe me.

142
00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:16.840
We looked.

143
00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.630
Yep, if there was something
else down there,

144
00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:20.800
we would've found it.

145
00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.520
The ship was in terrible shape,

146
00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:26.860
all jacked up like it had maybe
been attacked and raided.

147
00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.660
Or perhaps a mutiny
had broken out

148
00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:30.660
and they all killed each
other in a violent struggle

149
00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.990
for power and survival.

150
00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:46.630
Look around, boys!

151
00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.880
This is exactly why
we need more information!

152
00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.840
Intelligence means the
difference between life

153
00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:52.010
and death for this whole crew

154
00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.740
and if we're going
to sail to sky island,

155
00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.950
then we need
information to stay alive

156
00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.780
or whatever happened to that
ship could happen to us too!

157
00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.860
We didn't brave giant monsters
so you could bring back

158
00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.120
a creepy octopus, some rusty
swords, and a broken dish!

159
00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.530
This is all junk!

160
00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:07.280
And you're all idiots!

161
00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:11.700
What is that, Luffy?

162
00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.620
[LUFFY]
Armor!

163
00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:16.370
[crash]

164
00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:18.240
Whoa! She crushed the armor!

165
00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:19.980
Nami, you didn't even
notice the pretty sea shells

166
00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.310
I brought you!

167
00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:23.210
Cram your sea shells
in your shorts!

168
00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.200
She's so beautiful
when she's angry.

169
00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.290
You should still try
to keep your distance.

170
00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:31.610
[ROBIN]
Bad day, huh?

171
00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.780
[NAMI]
It's only going to get
worse working with these guys.

172
00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.490
We'll never figure out how
that ship sailed to the sky.

173
00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.800
I'm gonna snap on
them any second.

174
00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.600
[ROBIN]
Maybe this'll help.

175
00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.800
Eternal Pose?

176
00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.800
But how?

177
00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.550
Oh, I took it off that
salvager's ship earlier.

178
00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:48.380
Just in case.

179
00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.940
[NAMI laughs]

180
00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.720
You're the only one
I can depend on!

181
00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.760
[LUFFY]
All right, who's up
for an octopus dinner tonight?

182
00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.400
That boy has got
to learn to relax.

183
00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.350
[NAMI]
Jaya?

184
00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.350
This must have
been their home port.

185
00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.820
Jaya? Is that where
we're going next?

186
00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:17.990
That would be your
decision, Captain!

187
00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:23.040
All hands, on deck!

188
00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.550
Set our course to Jaya!

189
00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.800
So, uh, any of you know
which direction that might be?

190
00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:32.930
[NAMI]
Starboard.

191
00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.560
[LUFFY]
You heard her, Chopper!

192
00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.250
[CHOPPER]
Right!

193
00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.890
[LUFFY]
Onward to Jaya!

194
00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:39.340
[USOPP]
Hmm?

195
00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.320
Now hold up just a minute.

196
00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.680
If we head off to this Jaya
place that's so important,

197
00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.430
won't the Log Pose's needle
change its position again?

198
00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:51.050
[USOPP]
'Cause if that happens,

199
00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:53.010
we won't know which
direction sky island is.

200
00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:53.800
What?

201
00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.800
All hands, full stop!

202
00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.800
Wanna tell me why you're
messing with my head Nami?

203
00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:58.970
I'm not.

204
00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.400
You're the genius who
decided we should go to Jaya.

205
00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.480
Oh yeah, that's right.

206
00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.390
Well, I didn't know
it was gonna ruin our plans

207
00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:05.640
to get to this Skypiea.

208
00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.930
It's not my fault you have
the memory of a goldfish.

209
00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:11.060
Think, the Log Pose has always
worked that way, hasn't it?

210
00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:12.560
Yeah, I guess so.

211
00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.960
Hey! Listen up!

212
00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.290
I have an important
announcement to make!

213
00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:19.590
Seeing as I'm the captain, I say
we set our course for Skypiea!

214
00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:20.920
How do you propose we get there?

215
00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:23.180
We're gonna have to
ask for some directions.

216
00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:25.390
Maybe someone in
Jaya will know the way.

217
00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:26.810
Very well, Jaya it is.

218
00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:30.020
Right! On to Jaya!

219
00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:32.470
You already said that!

220
00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:33.920
I doubt that the
needle would change

221
00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.800
as soon as we get there.

222
00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:37.300
So why don't we pull into port

223
00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:39.880
and then leave before it
has a chance to adjust?

224
00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:40.590
Sounds good to me.

225
00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.300
If we're lucky, it'll work.

226
00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.320
That sounds like a plan to us.

227
00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:47.530
[LUFFY]
Full sail to Jaya, people!

228
00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:50.010
And this time it's for real!

229
00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:52.810
[NAMI]
Now stop stuffing
your faces and get to work!

230
00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.960
[CHOPPER]
I wonder
what this Jaya place is like.

231
00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.210
I hope it's relaxing.

232
00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.210
[SANJI]
Nami my sweet!

233
00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.670
Robin my dear!

234
00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.000
Dinner is served.

235
00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:15.480
<b>Roshio "the Executioner"
Captain of the Roshio Pirates
Bounty: 42 Million Belly</b>

236
00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.840
[ROSHIO]
Looks like that's
the last of your cash.

237
00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:12.630
But if you wanted to...

238
00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.470
...I'd let you raise with, say

239
00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:15.480
your clothes.

240
00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.480
[MEDDLER B]
You're lucky
and you don't even know it.

241
00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:18.470
[MEDDLER A]
Playing with Roshio,

242
00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:20.010
even if you would
have won the hand,

243
00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.230
trust me, you would
have lost something else.

244
00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:26.370
[ROSHIO]
I suppose
that about wraps it up.

245
00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:29.820
[BELLAMY]
Don't think so.

246
00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.080
You cheated this entire hand,

247
00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.830
didn't you?

248
00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.290
I never cheat.

249
00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.540
You're a liar.

250
00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:37.870
You lie.

251
00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.880
I watched every
deceitful move you made.

252
00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.550
[ROSHIO]
You better watch you
mouth in this place, loser!

253
00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:45.230
Sarquiss?

254
00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:47.160
Hey, Sarquiss!

255
00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:47.950
[SARQUISS]
Hmm?

256
00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:48.890
What is it?

257
00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:52.080
[BELLAMY]
This guy was cheating just now.

258
00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:54.790
You saw the whole
thing, didn't you?

259
00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:55.960
[SARQUISS]
You bet I did.

260
00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.210
Every rotten little move.

261
00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:58.910
He cheated straight through.

262
00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:00.790
I say we do something
about this guy.

263
00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.290
Make an example out of him.

264
00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:05.490
You have no idea
who you're dealing with!

265
00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:32.770
<b>Bellamy "the Hyena"
Captain of the Bellamy Pirates
Bounty: 55 Million Belly</b>

266
00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:31.110
[giggles]

267
00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:35.100
You see anything, Usopp?

268
00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:36.030
Nothing.

269
00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.570
Just the sky and the sea.

270
00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.240
I thought that
Jaya Island wasn't too far

271
00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:40.560
from where we were.

272
00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.450
[NAMI]
It shouldn't be.

273
00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:43.490
And with the weather
being so clear.

274
00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:46.080
We should have spotted
the coastline over an hour ago.

275
00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.950
I'm gonna like Jaya
if it's as warm as it is now.

276
00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.710
I'm finally getting
to work on my tan.

277
00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.870
Spring weather's the best.

278
00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:59.080
It looks like the seagulls
are enjoying it too.

279
00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:10.510
They've been shot!

280
00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:12.860
Looks like we'll be
eating good tonight.

281
00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:14.690
I don't think they could
have been shot, Chopper.

282
00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.470
I didn't hear any gunfire.

283
00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:17.520
I found a bullet!

284
00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.140
And judging from the trajectory
it came from that way!

285
00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:21.180
[NAMI]
Are you saying the shots

286
00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:23.810
came from an island we
can't even see yet?

287
00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:25.520
That's impossible, Chopper.

288
00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:27.610
But I saw it happen
with my own eyes!

289
00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:28.610
[laughs]

290
00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.320
A tuna had a better
chance at killing them.

291
00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.720
No sniper or gun
has that kind of range.

292
00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:35.550
They were probably shot before
and just happened to fall now.

293
00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:36.800
Hey, Sanji!

294
00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:39.310
Look! We found our dinner!

295
00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:47.310
[OGRE]
Poor creature.

296
00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:48.640
He must have suffered.

297
00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:51.720
<b>West Coast, Jaya</b>

298
00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:51.720
I wasn't able to get an
instant kill on one of them.

299
00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.920
But that's what
fate haled for him.

300
00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.630
All the events of his life
destined him to this outcome,

301
00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:59.080
so I can't blame myself.

302
00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:06.960
[BURGESS]
Hey, jerk!

303
00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.870
Do you know who I am?

304
00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.880
No! Get lost.

305
00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:11.580
Ha!

306
00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.710
I'll tell ya!

307
00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.680
I'm the greatest fighting
champion ever!

308
00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:19.780
[LUFFY]
Haha! Awesome!

309
00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:22.360
Check it out,
this town looks great!

310
00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:25.090
Is it just me or does this
place look like a resort?

311
00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:26.090
It sure does!

312
00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.590
Hurry up and dock!

313
00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.220
It does look promising.

314
00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:32.040
Maybe we can even
stay here awhile.

315
00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:33.460
[USOPP]
Hmm?

316
00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:38.800
[USOPP]
Either I'm
starting to hallucinate

317
00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:41.460
or the harbor over there
is full of pirate ships.

318
00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:42.540
[NAMI]
Don't be silly, Usopp!

319
00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:45.040
Since when can pirates
dock their ships in a harbor

320
00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:46.590
without being run out of town.

321
00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:50.550
[USOPP chuckles]
You're right. It must be a joke.

322
00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:51.380
Someone help!

323
00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:52.380
He's gonna kill me!

324
00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.490
What the heck's going
on with this crazy town?

325
00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.760
[BURGESS laughs]

326
00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.920
What a pathetic little weakling!

327
00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:03.470
[DRUNK]
Hu‐ho! Mister you picked
the wrong guy to beat up.

328
00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:05.310
Look at that emblem.

329
00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.330
He's in Roshio's gang.

330
00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.130
You have heard of Roshio, right?

331
00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:13.340
You know, the executioner whose
bounty is 42 million Berries!

332
00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:17.790
The man is psychotic,
you better watch your back!

333
00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:19.210
[CUSTOMER A]
That guy is full of it.

334
00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:21.210
We watched that
entire game ourselves.

335
00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.300
No one cheated.

336
00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:23.460
I still can't believe
he was able

337
00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.420
to beat up Roshio so easily.

338
00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.340
Don't you know?
That's Bellamy.

339
00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.130
[CUSTOMER B]
What? That's Bellamy?

340
00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:32.910
The one with the 55 million
bounty on his head?

341
00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:34.780
Captain!

342
00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:35.780
I can't believe it!

343
00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:36.950
Who did this to him?

344
00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.830
[UNDERLING B]
We need
to get him to a doctor! Hurry!

345
00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:39.830
[UNDERLING C]
Hang in there, Captain!

346
00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:41.930
We'll get ya' fixed up!

347
00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:00.200
Now this looks
like my kind of town.

348
00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:03.260
[ZORO]
We'll have
no problem fitting in here.

349
00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:04.800
There's no way.

350
00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:06.410
Do you think those
two can last an hour

351
00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:08.010
without getting
into any trouble?

352
00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:09.760
Well, by the
looks of this place,

353
00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:12.260
I'd say 15 minutes
is a generous assumption.

354
00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:13.770
You really think so?

355
00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:14.870
I'd better save them!

356
00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:15.670
Nami!

357
00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:16.960
[NAMI]
Luffy! Zoro!

358
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:17.710
Wait for me!

359
00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:19.120
I'm coming too!

360
00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:21.620
There she goes.

361
00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:23.260
Don't worry.
I'm sure she'll be fine

362
00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.260
with those two protecting her.

363
00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:26.600
[SANJI]
I'm the only
one who can protect Nami.

364
00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:27.680
[USOPP]
Not today!

365
00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.170
Nami will be safe and
sound with Luffy and Zoro!

366
00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.920
But if you leave, then what
are we supposed to do

367
00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.110
– if the ship is attacked?
– Please don't leave!

368
00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.630
Who's gonna protect us?

369
00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.090
Fine, I'll stay behind.

370
00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.150
Let me go!

371
00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.400
Ha.

372
00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:41.320
I guess I'll whip up some tea
and hold down the fort then.

373
00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:42.240
Where did Robin go?

374
00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:43.840
Huh?

375
00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.220
I don't know.

376
00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:47.010
[USOPP]
Sanji, about that tea.

377
00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:48.430
[SANJI]
Make it yourself.

378
00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:52.980
I got my tough face on
so if anybody messes with...

379
00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.340
[NAMI]
No fighting! Promise me!

380
00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.180
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

381
00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:57.430
I promise.

382
00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.470
Good. This is serious
business you two.

383
00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:01.140
– Good.
– Great.

384
00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.040
[NAMI]
Gee, thanks for the support!

385
00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:05.220
Look, if one of you
causes trouble here,

386
00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:07.050
we'll have to get
out of this town.

387
00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:08.260
And if that happens,

388
00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:10.850
then we'll never know how to
get to the sky island, right?

389
00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:12.430
[LUFFY]
Yeah.

390
00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:14.520
Whoa. He's messed up.

391
00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:16.180
[LUFFY]
Looks like
he fell off his horse.

392
00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:17.720
[ZORO]
That's gotta hurt.

393
00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.580
[LUFFY]
Looks like he's in pain too.

394
00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:23.100
[ZORO]
No doubt.

395
00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.860
Hey. Sorry to bother you.

396
00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.360
But will you help me up?

397
00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:29.940
[ZORO]
What, are you not
in the mood to help yourself?

398
00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:31.820
Luffy. Give me a hand.

399
00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.280
Sure.

400
00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:35.000
Up you go!

401
00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.750
[DOC Q]
Hey, would ya look at that!

402
00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.450
I'm on my horse again.

403
00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:42.380
I was a sickly child growing
up and never got better.

404
00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:45.430
Now let's get out
of here, Stronger.

405
00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:47.100
[LUFFY, ZORO]
– The horse too?
– The horse too?

406
00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:50.060
[ZORO]
We should put them
out of their misery.

407
00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.270
[DOC Q]
Thanks again, pal.

408
00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:52.780
Ya know I don't
have enough money

409
00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.330
for a reward these days,

410
00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.370
but care for an apple?

411
00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:57.350
[ZORO]
Do you take us for idiots?

412
00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:59.480
We'd never trust food
from someone like you.

413
00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.150
Hey, look! Apples!

414
00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:04.950
Luffy!

415
00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.190
What the? What happened?

416
00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:08.350
[CLERK]
Some guys
took a few apples

417
00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:09.560
from that freak on the horse,

418
00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:13.100
and when they bit into
them, they exploded!

419
00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:16.980
Oh no! Luffy! Spit it out!

420
00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:18.600
Spit out the apple you just ate!

421
00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:21.150
I already swallowed it!

422
00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.330
What the hell'd you do that for?

423
00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:25.290
[laughs]

424
00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.280
No worries.

425
00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:27.990
The boy isn't hurt.

426
00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.740
[MAN C]
What happened?

427
00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:32.340
[MAN D]
I don't know,
but the inside's destroyed.

428
00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.710
[DOC Q]
If you had
eaten the bad one,

429
00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.590
you would have died
on the first bite.

430
00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.840
Heh! You're lucky.

431
00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:45.090
[ONLOOKER A]
What is all this?

432
00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:48.140
[ONLOOKER B]
It's Roshio's grave now.

433
00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.390
[ONLOOKER A]
It looks like
a war broke out here.

434
00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:53.390
Did they fire a cannon into
the middle of town or something?

435
00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.520
[ONLOOKER B]
Who knows?

436
00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.600
Even the people who were
there and saw what happened

437
00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:59.210
said they couldn't tell
exactly what was going on.

438
00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:02.000
About the only thing
everyone knows for certain

439
00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:04.250
is that Bellamy had
something to do with this.

440
00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:05.330
[ONLOOKER A]
Bellamy the Hyena?

441
00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:07.210
I think it's pretty obvious

442
00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:10.090
that he's using the power
of one of the devil's fruits.

443
00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:15.050
[NAMI]
What's the deal with this town?

444
00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:16.110
I don't know.

445
00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:17.700
Who really cares?

446
00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:18.740
You should care

447
00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:21.040
seeing as you were
almost killed for no reason.

448
00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:23.660
Well that was bound to
happen sooner or later.

449
00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.000
Have you lost your mind?

450
00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.800
[BURGESS roars]

451
00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:30.840
[laughs]

452
00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.180
Oh great, look who's back.

453
00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.760
How many victims
has he racked up now?

454
00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:37.060
[MAN E]
It's not like he's
a famous fugitive or anything.

455
00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.230
Who do you think he is?

456
00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:40.980
I don't care, and to be honest,
I don't want to know.

457
00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:43.520
If that meathead wants
to be the fighting champion,

458
00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.440
then go ahead and let him.

459
00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:47.640
Fighting champion?

460
00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:51.100
Hey, don't even
think about it you two!

461
00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.100
Dammit.

462
00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:53.060
I'm starting to wonder

463
00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:56.390
if we can find any
useful information here.

464
00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:00.220
[ZORO]
How about this place?

465
00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:03.450
[LUFFY]
Uh, seems pretty quiet to me.

466
00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:05.200
You can say that again.

467
00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:06.640
This place is gorgeous!

468
00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.410
To think such an oasis exists

469
00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:11.460
in the middle of
this disgusting town.

470
00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:12.460
[ZORO]
It's built above the water.

471
00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:14.630
[LUFFY]
That's great,
but there's no one here.

472
00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:16.980
Although I can smell
that someone's cooking.

473
00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:19.880
Excuse me!

474
00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:23.170
Excuse me! I'm gonna have to
ask you all to leave please.

475
00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:25.940
See, the entire hotel has been
rented out by Mr. Bellamy

476
00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:27.060
and his guests,
and he's asked that we

477
00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:29.780
tell other guests like
yourselves to go somewhere else.

478
00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:32.660
So, uh, you must understand that
I have no say in the matter.

479
00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:34.860
So, one man rented
out this entire place?

480
00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:36.110
If Mr. Bellamy sees you here,

481
00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.870
he'll have my head
removed from my body,

482
00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:40.130
so please leave for my sake.

483
00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:42.480
[LUFFY]
C'mon, I'm sure he won't mind.

484
00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:44.010
Who is this Bellamy anyway?

485
00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:46.150
[SARQUISS]
What's going on in here?

486
00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:49.370
Who are these scumbags and what
are they doing in our hotel?

487
00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:50.240
Mr. Sarquiss!

488
00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:51.240
Welcome back!

489
00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:52.950
I told them to leave,
but they won't listen!

490
00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:56.810
<b>"Big Knife" Sarquiss
First Mate, Bellamy Pirates
Bounty: 36 Million Belly</b>

491
00:22:52.990 --> 00:22:53.770
I really don't care.

492
00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:54.730
Just get rid of them!

493
00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:57.480
We're paying a lot of money
to have this place to ourselves.

494
00:22:57.520 --> 00:22:58.430
She's right.

495
00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:00.730
Now get out of here
before I throw you out.

496
00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:02.810
Hey, guys, would you
mind if I beat him up?

497
00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:03.940
Luffy!

498
00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:06.780
Ha! You're going to beat me up?

499
00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:09.110
[laughs]
Hilarious!

500
00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:10.640
Here.

501
00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:13.850
Go buy some new rags so you
don't look like an orphan.

502
00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:15.230
[LILY]
Sarquiss,
you're wasting your money

503
00:23:15.270 --> 00:23:17.100
by tossing it to
this bunch of losers.

504
00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:18.270
[SARQUISS]
No kidding.

505
00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:20.940
I should have just flushed it
down along with my lunch.

506
00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:22.040
I'll take free money!

507
00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.360
Let's go.

508
00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.980
These jerks can't help us.

509
00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:27.030
[LUFFY]
I can walk on my own, you know.

510
00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:28.880
See you around.

511
00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:31.420
[EDDY]
Sarquiss. Lily.

512
00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:32.850
Just leave well enough alone.

513
00:23:33.690 --> 00:23:36.230
[SARQUISS]
Eddy,
we've been looking for you.

514
00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:38.400
You know that
trash you ran into?

515
00:23:38.440 --> 00:23:41.320
Seems that they've been doing
pretty well for themselves.

516
00:23:41.350 --> 00:23:42.250
Look.

517
00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:43.310
Not bad,

518
00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:44.740
but they're nothing compared
to you and Bellamy.

519
00:23:44.740 --> 00:23:45.700
Here.

520
00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:51.530
<b>The Bellamy Pirates</b>

521
00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:47.790
But for ordinary scum
they can hold their own.

522
00:23:47.830 --> 00:23:48.950
They still don't stand

523
00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.750
a chance of surviving the
transition into the new era.

524
00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:52.830
Wow.

525
00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:56.940
His bounty is 30 million,
for such a little puke.

526
00:23:56.980 --> 00:24:00.190
I'm sure Bellamy
will want to see this.

527
00:24:00.570 --> 00:24:02.950
Man, that really pisses me off!

528
00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:04.190
[TERRY]
That's a shame.

529
00:24:04.230 --> 00:24:05.400
Cause you know.

530
00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:07.990
Mock Town's economy depends
on pirates throwing money around

531
00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:10.320
to show off power they
may or may not have.

532
00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:13.490
What, so poor pirates aren't
allowed on the island?

533
00:24:13.530 --> 00:24:15.950
Looks like there's
no way of calming you down.

534
00:24:15.950 --> 00:24:18.290
Here. This one's on the house.

535
00:24:18.330 --> 00:24:19.070
Huh?

536
00:24:19.070 --> 00:24:20.190
[TERRY]
Tough guys and degenerates

537
00:24:20.190 --> 00:24:22.990
are our clientele here,
so trouble isn't hard to find.

538
00:24:22.990 --> 00:24:25.740
You aren't gonna make it in this
town if ya let it bother ya.

539
00:24:25.790 --> 00:24:28.160
You have to play it
safe when you can.

540
00:24:28.180 --> 00:24:29.720
Here you go.

541
00:24:29.790 --> 00:24:31.960
This whole town's
a real dump, ya know?

542
00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:34.130
Of course, that's how
most level‐headed people

543
00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:34.980
would think of it.

544
00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:35.980
But unfortunately for you,

545
00:24:35.980 --> 00:24:38.740
level‐headed people
are rare in these parts.

546
00:24:38.790 --> 00:24:41.340
The wanted posters won't be on
the walls for a couple of days,

547
00:24:41.380 --> 00:24:44.920
so you may want to skip town
sooner rather than later.

548
00:24:44.970 --> 00:24:46.010
A couple days.

549
00:24:46.050 --> 00:24:48.090
That doesn't give us much time.

550
00:24:48.140 --> 00:24:49.050
Now here's a question.

551
00:24:49.090 --> 00:24:50.300
– Hey, fatso!
– [BLACKBEARD] Hey, barkeep!

552
00:24:50.350 --> 00:24:51.220
[TERRY]
Huh?

553
00:24:51.300 --> 00:24:52.470
What's wrong?

554
00:24:52.510 --> 00:24:53.680
– [BLACKBEARD] This cherry pie
– [LUFFY] This cherry pie

555
00:24:53.740 --> 00:24:55.160
– tastes friggin' delicious!
– tastes friggin' horrible!

556
00:24:55.180 --> 00:24:56.470
– Huh?
– Hm?

557
00:25:05.350 --> 00:25:06.560
– This is one of the
– This is one of the

558
00:25:06.610 --> 00:25:09.190
– worst drinks I've ever tasted!
– best drinks I've ever tasted!

559
00:25:09.890 --> 00:25:11.390
I think there
may be something wrong

560
00:25:11.420 --> 00:25:13.010
with your taste buds, kid.

561
00:25:13.050 --> 00:25:16.050
I think there's somethin' wrong
with your big fat head.

562
00:25:16.090 --> 00:25:17.890
Well, I'm not
the cook in this joint,

563
00:25:17.930 --> 00:25:19.800
so I don't care
what you have to say.

564
00:25:19.850 --> 00:25:21.140
Got it?

565
00:25:21.180 --> 00:25:24.180
Hey, barkeep!
I'll take 50 steaks to go!

566
00:25:24.230 --> 00:25:27.520
And I'll take 51 of those
delicious cherry pies to go.

567
00:25:27.560 --> 00:25:29.940
Wait, make that 52 steaks!

568
00:25:29.940 --> 00:25:31.550
[BLACKBEARD]
Better make that 53 pies.

569
00:25:31.640 --> 00:25:33.050
[LUFFY]
Fifty‐four steaks!

570
00:25:33.100 --> 00:25:34.350
[BLACKBEARD]
Fifty‐five pies!

571
00:25:34.390 --> 00:25:35.520
[LUFFY]
Sixty steaks!

572
00:25:35.560 --> 00:25:36.600
[BLACKBEARD]
Seventy pies!

573
00:25:36.600 --> 00:25:37.220
[LUFFY]
Eighty!

574
00:25:37.220 --> 00:25:38.140
[BLACKBEARD]
A hundred!

575
00:25:38.170 --> 00:25:40.940
I'm gonna beat the
living crap out of you!

576
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:42.290
Do you two even
have the slightest idea

577
00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:43.210
what you're fighting about?

578
00:25:43.250 --> 00:25:45.030
Luffy, you promised, remember?

579
00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:47.930
Besides, we don't have enough
money to buy dozens of steaks!

580
00:25:47.950 --> 00:25:49.780
We aren't here to shop!

581
00:25:49.870 --> 00:25:51.990
So then, are you a pirate?

582
00:25:51.990 --> 00:25:54.000
Yeah. That's right.

583
00:25:54.040 --> 00:25:55.440
How big's your bounty?

584
00:25:55.440 --> 00:25:57.420
Thirty million.

585
00:25:57.420 --> 00:26:00.260
Thirty million? For you?

586
00:26:00.320 --> 00:26:02.540
I wouldn't believe it
even if I collected it!

587
00:26:02.560 --> 00:26:04.940
Are you calling me
a liar you fat, hairy ape?

588
00:26:04.980 --> 00:26:05.960
[ZORO]
Enough!

589
00:26:06.190 --> 00:26:07.520
[TERRY]
We've got rules in this place,

590
00:26:07.570 --> 00:26:09.340
and one of 'em's no fighting.

591
00:26:09.340 --> 00:26:13.260
Here's your 50 cherry pies.
Now please, just walk away.

592
00:26:32.200 --> 00:26:35.030
[BELLAMY]
I'm looking for a
pirate that wears a straw hat.

593
00:26:35.080 --> 00:26:37.040
[LUFFY]
Hmm?

594
00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:39.330
[CUSTOMER A]
It's Bellamy!

595
00:26:43.250 --> 00:26:45.380
So you must
be Straw Hat Luffy,

596
00:26:45.420 --> 00:26:47.340
worth a cool 30 million.

597
00:26:47.380 --> 00:26:48.340
Who's this guy?

598
00:26:48.380 --> 00:26:50.920
Looks like he has a bone
to pick with you, Luffy.

599
00:26:50.970 --> 00:26:52.120
That must be that Bellamy guy

600
00:26:52.120 --> 00:26:54.210
that rented out
the hotel we were at.

601
00:26:54.240 --> 00:26:54.940
Did you hear that?

602
00:26:54.940 --> 00:26:56.720
The kid's worth 30 million.

603
00:26:57.190 --> 00:26:57.700
[CUSTOMER C]
No way.

604
00:26:58.410 --> 00:26:59.450
[CUSTOMER B]
Tell me about it.

605
00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:02.580
How come everyone
I meet in this town is so tall?

606
00:27:02.610 --> 00:27:04.650
I'll take a glass
from the top shelf

607
00:27:04.690 --> 00:27:07.570
and give the kid
whatever he wants.

608
00:27:07.610 --> 00:27:09.110
Right.

609
00:27:09.900 --> 00:27:11.160
[SARQUISS]
Look at this place.

610
00:27:11.200 --> 00:27:13.110
This joint is packed solid!

611
00:27:13.740 --> 00:27:15.080
[LILY]
This place is disgusting.

612
00:27:15.120 --> 00:27:16.370
It smells like vomit.

613
00:27:16.410 --> 00:27:18.540
[RIVERS]
All you can
get here is cheap rum.

614
00:27:18.550 --> 00:27:19.250
Look, Zoro.

615
00:27:19.250 --> 00:27:21.420
It's those guys from earlier.

616
00:27:23.270 --> 00:27:24.310
You'd be in a lot less pain

617
00:27:24.330 --> 00:27:27.000
if you'd just offered
us your seats.

618
00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:28.380
Pathetic harbor trash.

619
00:27:32.630 --> 00:27:35.320
[CUSTOMER D]
It's him! "Big Knife" Sarquiss!

620
00:27:35.340 --> 00:27:38.300
[CUSTOMER E]
How much you wanna
bet he's looking for a fight?

621
00:27:38.300 --> 00:27:40.390
[CUSTOMER D]
Oh great.

622
00:27:40.440 --> 00:27:41.610
The whole gang is here.

623
00:27:41.650 --> 00:27:44.150
There's no way that they stopped
in just for a bite to eat.

624
00:27:44.190 --> 00:27:44.890
Drop it, man.

625
00:27:44.900 --> 00:27:46.990
It has nothing to do with us.

626
00:27:47.070 --> 00:27:49.030
What's Bellamy up to?

627
00:27:49.030 --> 00:27:50.190
[SARQUISS]
The usual fun.

628
00:27:52.410 --> 00:27:53.580
[BELLAMY]
Cheers.

629
00:27:53.580 --> 00:27:57.280
Hey, thanks for the drink, pal!
You know what? You're all right.

630
00:28:01.600 --> 00:28:08.500
[CUSTOMER F]
He did it!

631
00:28:08.710 --> 00:28:10.550
[laughs]

632
00:28:10.590 --> 00:28:11.880
Brilliant move, Bellamy!

633
00:28:11.920 --> 00:28:13.050
Just brilliant!

634
00:28:13.050 --> 00:28:14.550
[laughs]

635
00:28:14.590 --> 00:28:17.050
Huh?

636
00:28:17.050 --> 00:28:18.930
What are you doing, punk?

637
00:28:21.310 --> 00:28:24.560
[ZORO]
That's the question
you should be asking yourself.

638
00:28:26.570 --> 00:28:28.270
Zoro! Don't do it!

639
00:28:28.270 --> 00:28:30.230
We still need to get
some information from...

640
00:28:30.230 --> 00:28:33.530
Quiet! If this guy wants
a fight, I'll give it to him.

641
00:28:36.410 --> 00:28:38.450
[BELLAMY]
So that's all
you've got for backup?

642
00:28:38.610 --> 00:28:42.230
[laughs]

643
00:28:42.280 --> 00:28:45.250
Now, are you ready
to take me on or not?

644
00:28:45.780 --> 00:28:46.800
Heh...

645
00:28:46.800 --> 00:28:47.720
[CUSTOMER G]
No way!

646
00:28:47.760 --> 00:28:50.230
The kid just challenged Bellamy!

647
00:28:51.810 --> 00:28:53.440
[CUSTOMER I]
He'll be slaughtered!

648
00:28:53.480 --> 00:28:54.770
[laughs]

649
00:28:54.910 --> 00:28:57.330
You've got it all wrong, kid.
This isn't a fight.

650
00:28:57.430 --> 00:28:58.330
It's a test.

651
00:28:58.330 --> 00:29:00.590
Now come on.
Let's see how strong you are.

652
00:29:00.590 --> 00:29:02.350
Luffy, hold on!

653
00:29:02.350 --> 00:29:04.520
Mister, we're trying
to get to the sky island.

654
00:29:04.630 --> 00:29:07.470
Do you know anything about that?

655
00:29:11.600 --> 00:29:14.520
Did she just say "sky island"?

656
00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:15.940
She's crazy.

657
00:29:24.410 --> 00:29:27.330
[NAMI]
Like I was saying, if you
know how to get to sky island...

658
00:29:27.330 --> 00:29:34.090
[laughter]

659
00:29:34.130 --> 00:29:36.220
Did she say
what I think she said?

660
00:29:37.840 --> 00:29:40.180
Sky island? What an idiot!

661
00:29:40.220 --> 00:29:41.050
What the...

662
00:29:41.090 --> 00:29:42.720
You can look at the
Log Pose yourself!

663
00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:45.720
It's pointed at the sky,
plain as day!

664
00:29:45.810 --> 00:29:46.980
[CUSTOMER I]
Hey, check it out!

665
00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:52.900
Do I look like the Log Pose now?

666
00:29:53.180 --> 00:29:55.100
[CUSTOMER J]
No one trusts
those things anymore!

667
00:29:55.140 --> 00:29:56.520
They break if you breathe wrong!

668
00:29:56.560 --> 00:29:58.690
[laughs]

669
00:29:58.730 --> 00:30:00.480
You got me there, kid.

670
00:30:00.520 --> 00:30:01.690
I can't believe you
guys are putting hope

671
00:30:01.730 --> 00:30:07.160
into such a ridiculous legend
like an island in the sky.

672
00:30:07.160 --> 00:30:09.490
Especially considering
how little you know.

673
00:30:09.540 --> 00:30:11.370
Like, of the thousands
of weird currents cutting

674
00:30:11.410 --> 00:30:12.460
through the Grand Line,

675
00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:16.170
one of the weirdest is
called the Knock‐Up Stream.

676
00:30:16.240 --> 00:30:17.830
Looks to me like
this is the first

677
00:30:17.870 --> 00:30:19.790
you've ever heard about it.

678
00:30:19.840 --> 00:30:22.220
Any ship that gets caught
in the Knock‐Up Stream

679
00:30:22.220 --> 00:30:23.840
is catapulted into the sky,

680
00:30:23.880 --> 00:30:26.800
and later slams back
into the ocean.

681
00:30:26.850 --> 00:30:29.350
Years ago, a bunch
of ignorant sailors saw

682
00:30:29.430 --> 00:30:31.140
ships falling from the sky

683
00:30:31.190 --> 00:30:33.810
and assumed there must be
an island up there somewhere.

684
00:30:33.860 --> 00:30:37.820
In their minds, how else could
a ship get up that high? Ha!

685
00:30:37.850 --> 00:30:38.770
Ridiculous!

686
00:30:38.810 --> 00:30:40.400
Anything that seems supernatural

687
00:30:40.400 --> 00:30:42.610
always has a
rational explanation.

688
00:30:42.650 --> 00:30:45.490
Anything a man can dream
will eventually be explained,

689
00:30:45.570 --> 00:30:47.900
and let me tell ya,
the truth will hurt.

690
00:30:47.950 --> 00:30:49.420
What a shame.

691
00:30:49.420 --> 00:30:50.120
Look.

692
00:30:50.120 --> 00:30:51.540
I was gonna let you join my crew

693
00:30:51.580 --> 00:30:53.460
if you'd passed the
test of the new era.

694
00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:57.170
But it seems like
you're a lost cause.

695
00:30:57.220 --> 00:31:00.550
Thing is, the time of
pirate's dreams are over!

696
00:31:00.590 --> 00:31:04.260
The City of Gold, the Emerald
Ruins, and the great One Piece!

697
00:31:04.300 --> 00:31:06.560
The fools who dream of
these fictional treasures

698
00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:09.480
don't notice the real
treasures that surround them!

699
00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:12.390
In this age of oceans, the very
men who are brave enough

700
00:31:12.440 --> 00:31:14.690
and capable of
navigating currents end up

701
00:31:14.730 --> 00:31:18.610
chasing these ridiculous
dreams and die in the process!

702
00:31:18.650 --> 00:31:21.570
Whenever people speak of these
dead idiots they always say,

703
00:31:21.610 --> 00:31:24.330
"He was happy because
he died living his dreams."

704
00:31:24.330 --> 00:31:25.080
Ha!

705
00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:28.130
No, he died because
he was a fool!

706
00:31:28.170 --> 00:31:31.130
So when I see people
chasing dreams of One Piece,

707
00:31:31.170 --> 00:31:33.720
I get disgusted!

708
00:31:33.720 --> 00:31:35.090
[NAMI]
Luffy!

709
00:31:36.880 --> 00:31:39.640
[BELLAMY]
You're a weak pirate,
just like they were,

710
00:31:39.680 --> 00:31:42.430
and as long as you're hacking
around, you'll make us,

711
00:31:42.470 --> 00:31:45.310
the real pirates,
look like trash.

712
00:31:46.730 --> 00:31:47.550
[CUSTOMER K chuckles]

713
00:31:47.550 --> 00:31:49.550
Get out of here,
you scrawny punk!

714
00:31:49.620 --> 00:31:51.170
You're killing our buzz!

715
00:31:51.210 --> 00:31:52.930
Way to go, Bellamy!

716
00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:53.920
Get lost, you wimp!

717
00:31:53.960 --> 00:31:55.510
[CUSTOMER N]
Put him in a body bag, Bellamy!

718
00:31:55.550 --> 00:31:56.970
Yeah!

719
00:31:57.010 --> 00:31:57.930
[laughs]

720
00:31:58.160 --> 00:31:59.660
Bellamy, give
these people what they want!

721
00:31:59.950 --> 00:32:01.070
Tear into them!

722
00:32:01.660 --> 00:32:02.490
[BELLAMY chuckles]

723
00:32:02.530 --> 00:32:04.710
I'd be more than
happy to entertain.

724
00:32:04.710 --> 00:32:06.760
Yeah.

725
00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:07.880
Luffy! Zoro!

726
00:32:07.920 --> 00:32:08.760
Forget about all that
pacifist crap I was talking

727
00:32:08.800 --> 00:32:12.390
about earlier and
take this jerk out!

728
00:32:12.430 --> 00:32:14.140
[LUFFY]
Zoro.

729
00:32:15.520 --> 00:32:18.460
No matter what happens,
don't fight back.
